                           the Song of Songs; title and incipit of the daily readings of <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/>; title of
                           <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/>; name and traditional interpretation of the Hebrew letters in <ref cRef="betmas:LIT2000Mazmur.Ps118">Psalm 118</ref>; 
                           letters <foreign xml:lang="gez">ስ</foreign> and <foreign xml:lang="gez">ሕ</foreign> in the word <foreign xml:lang="gez">ስብሕዎ</foreign> in 
                           <ref cRef="betmas:LIT2000Mazmur.Ps150">Psalm 150</ref>; 
                           letters <foreign xml:lang="gez">ባ</foreign> and <foreign xml:lang="gez">ክ</foreign> of the
                           word <foreign xml:lang="gez">ይባርክዎ</foreign> in Canticle 10; refrains of <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/> (written out
                           fully or abbreviated); elements of the punctuation marks and text
                           dividers; Ethiopic numerals or their elements. Three groups of
                           lines (alternating with black lines) on the opening page of <ref target="#ms_i1.1"/>, <ref target="#ms_i1.2"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/>;
                          two groups of lines of the incipit of <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/>.</seg>
